## On the Ryzen (2026-11-28, bench-52)

Release 202611280807 = `claude/DRV-ryzen-bench-52-quiet-bt-wifi-refusal` 8b308d9df: `main` bd350b2f5 with this branch
and 700-BLT-0011. The QEMU groups "x86: boot, display, shell, memory, clock" and "x86: keys, shell, tools" passed on that
commit. The access point's 5 GHz network was on channel 40. The server stayed on the wire throughout.

- **Under UZ at the start:** `DATAPATH ADMITTED ON CHANNEL 40` at 6.2 s, joined.
- **`wifi country 00` at 67 s:** in data mode, `CHANNEL 40 NOT ALLOWED AT ITS ADMITTED POWER: SENDING SHOULD STOP; DEBUG
  MODE KEEPS SENDING` (data mode is not this task's).
- **`svc restart rtw89_wifi` at 85 s** (PID 22, then 53), so that the station meets the receive-only service under `00`:
  - `THE RADIO RESTARTED (IT HAS NO CHANNEL SET): ITS COUNTRY 00 AGAIN`;
  - the access point heard on listen-only channel 40;
  - then, once at 91.7 s: `CHANNEL 40 NOT ADMITTED: THE CALIBRATION'S 12 DBM IS ABOVE THE CHANNEL'S MAXIMUM UNDER THIS
    COUNTRY; THE STATION'S SENDS THERE ARE REFUSED UNTIL ITS COUNTRY CHANGES, THE RADIO STAYS UP RECEIVING`.
- **For the next 4.5 minutes:**
  - `wlan`'s tries 1 to 10 were answered `NO ANSWER`, at 10 s and then at 60 s apart;
  - `rtw89_wifi` stayed PID 53;
  - no `STOPPED CLEANLY`, no restart, no quarantine;
  - the refusal was not logged again.
- **`wifi country UZ` at 358 s:** `COUNTRY UZ: 21 CHANNELS`; at `wlan`'s next try (407.9 s) the calibration on 40 passed
  on both paths, then `DATAPATH ADMITTED ON CHANNEL 40`, `AUTO-JOIN CoolNet2: JOINED (TRY 11)`, DHCP on card 2.

Still not this task's: under `00` the station keeps trying the same network and does not fall back to its 2.4 GHz BSS
(`NET`'s, told on 2026-11-27).


## Related

- [213-DRV-0087](../issues/213-DRV-0087-rtl8852be-on-5-ghz.md): the 5 GHz work, and the second open item of its channel-40 section, which this is.
- `NET/2026-11-27T0547Z-DRV-the-access-point-moved-to-channel-40-under-00-the-station-loops-on-it-and-never-tries-2-4-ghz.md` on `internal-dev-messages`: the station's side.

## Resolution

`rtw89_wifi`'s serving loop asks the calibration's policy (`receive_service::admission`) before it admits a channel. The policy needs no RF write. If it refuses, the receive-only service:
- marks the channel and opens the filter again;
- logs `CHANNEL n NOT ADMITTED: <reason>` once;
- refuses every later send there at once, until a country is given again.

The radio stays up receiving. Before, the driver ended for a fresh start each time, until init quarantined it.

- **Host case:** `a_channel_the_policy_refuses_is_refused_to_the_station_and_the_radio_stays_up`, with its mutation check; `rtw89_service_host` 370 passed, `host_tests.sh` 282 ok.
- **On the Ryzen** (MC-12.1), bench-52 on 2026-11-28, with the access point on channel 40:
  - under `00`, after a restart of the driver: one `CHANNEL 40 NOT ADMITTED`, then 4.5 minutes of `wlan`'s tries refused with the same driver PID, no restart and no quarantine;
  - `UZ` again: joined on 40.
- **Left elsewhere:** the station's fallback to the 2.4 GHz BSS is `NET`'s.
